# abyss-net: the Wi-Fi netd helper of Abyss. Same binary as abyssd (/system_ext/bin/abyssd
# --net-helper), started by init with `seclabel u:r:abyss_net:s0`, `user system` (abyss.rc,
# service abyss-net), only while sys.abyss.wifi=on and Abyss is active.
#
# Why a separate process and domain: netd checks its callers' permissions; uid 1000 (system)
# passes at once, any other uid (root included) makes netd ask system_server's permission
# service and wait forever while system_server is stopped (system/netd/include/binder_utils/
# BinderUtil.h checkAnyPermission, frameworks/native/libs/binder/IServiceManager.cpp
# checkPermission). abyssd is uid root, so it never calls netd; it sends its requests here.
# Keeping the netd rights in this small domain also keeps them out of abyssd.
#
# Requests (abyssd/src/wifi/netcfg.rs): "up" = networkCreatePhysical(42) + networkAddInterface
# + interfaceAddAddress + networkAddRoute (subnet, default) + networkSetDefault; "down" =
# networkClearDefault + networkDestroy + interfaceClearAddrs; on SIGTERM also
# interfaceSetCfg(wlan0 "down").

type abyss_net, domain, coredomain;

# init -> abyss_net through the service's seclabel; the entrypoint is abyssd's executable.
# init_daemon_domain(abyssd) already makes init's default transition on abyssd_exec go to abyssd;
# an explicit seclabel overrides that type_transition, so only the allow rules are needed.
domain_trans(init, abyssd_exec, abyss_net)

# /dev/socket/abyss_net (init `socket abyss_net seqpacket 0660 system system`). abyssd connects
# (SOCK_SEQPACKET is the unix_stream_socket class); accept/read/write on the listening socket
# init created in our domain are granted to every domain (private/domain.te:30).
type abyss_net_socket, file_type, coredomain_socket;
unix_socket_connect(abyssd, abyss_net, abyss_net)

# netd's INetd binder service ("netd", netd_service).
binder_use(abyss_net)
# NEVERALLOW (hidden by SELINUX_IGNORE_NEVERALLOWS, listed in reports/impl-wifi.md):
# private/netd.te:174-181 lets only system_server, dumpstate, network_stack, netd and
# netutils_wrapper find netd_service. Abyss replaces ConnectivityService while system_server is
# stopped (DECISIONS "DNS/network in Abyss", 15:45), so this is the exception that decision
# planned for; it needs a matching `-abyss_net` in system/sepolicy before it can ship without the
# ignore flag. dnsresolver_service is NOT found (abyssd resolves its own names, wifi/dns.rs).
allow abyss_net netd_service:service_manager find;
# The calls themselves. The only binder neverallow on netd is for apps
# (private/netd.te:205 `neverallow { appdomain -network_stack } netd:binder call`).
binder_call(abyss_net, netd)
